/E (But we also know: under stress, you can't cook well, and you eat even worse. When our nervous system is on high alert, we swallow our food to fill up, not to feel. The flavor disappears. I am a chef, but I am also an intimacy and sex coach. To me, these two worlds are inseparable. Because those who can no longer taste at the table often can no longer fully feel in the bedroom.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [6]
>>
