/T (Today, we are going to take the pressure off completely. This mini-course is meant for one day, one evening: your date night. And my advice is: agree tonight that sex is off the table. That penetration is not on the menu. And that nothing "must" happen. After all, pressure is the ultimate sex killer. Consider this evening a first date where we dance on the edge of curiosity while guarding the peace and space. Agree on how far the other person can go, so that unconscious pressure falls away. You will notice that suddenly there is so much more to explore when the "destination" is scrapped. By removing the "destination > sex," the performance pressure disappears. You don't have to be afraid that a touch "has to mean something." You can just feel again.)
